{"parentUuid":"0ed56e4b-5ed0-4fee-9a8f-c3371697ac26","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4a5fe57a-4c8c-4d21-b38b-1de2c7cfd928","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XS1NuvXtw4zkfLGXrps22m","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntitle: \"Cybernaut-mini: scope decisions (2026-07-28)\"\ntags: [\"cybernaut\", \"planning\", \"kedro\", \"corpus\", \"docs\"]\ncreated: 2026-07-28T16:06:56.260Z\nupdated: 2026-07-28T16:06:56.260Z\nsources: []\nlinks: []\ncategory: decision\nconfidence: medium\nschemaVersion: 1\n---\n\n# Cybernaut-mini: scope decisions (2026-07-28)\n\nDecisions agreed with the user before planning the cybernaut-mini rebuild.\nReference blog: https://nosible.com/blog/the-road-to-cybernaut-1\nLocal copies: `data/00_reference/the-road-to-cybernaut-1.md` and `.build-guide.md`.\n\n## Goal\nReverse-engineer the NOSIBLE Cybernaut-1 retrieval stack as a *learning* repo.\nEvery component must carry direct blog references, stated assumptions, what the\ncode does to overcome them, and which alternatives were rejected and why.\n\n## Locked decisions\n\n1. **Layout — stage-numbered packages.** `build/` (Part A), `query/s1_language`\n   … `query/s8_retrieve` (Part B stages 1-8), `agent/` (Part C), `core/`\n   (rrf, models, config, trace). Splits the current `routing.py`, which today\n   fuses blog stages 5 AND 6 into one function.\n\n2. **Scope — all offline-capable NOT-BUILT components.** harmonic-TFIDF search\n   intents with POS filtering, instruction-template system, bloom filters,\n   trained zstd dictionaries, Aho-Corasick full-text intent pass, Bayesian dense\n   selector, Personalized PageRank reranker, prompt-injection rules,\n   multilingual stages 1-2. Neural reranker / LLM judge / LLM summaries stay\n   pluggable providers.\n\n3. **Corpus — REAL DATA ONLY. User was emphatic: \"THIS MUST NEVER USE DUMMY\n   DATA.\"** The existing 63-doc synthetic corpus and its fabricated judgments\n   are to be removed.\n   - Primary: BEIR SciFact (~5.2k real PubMed abstracts, real qrels,\n     CC BY-SA 4.0 as `BeIR/scifact`; note original `allenai/scifact` is tagged\n     CC BY-NC 2.0 — data needs its own attribution/licence file, not MIT).\n   - Multilingual: MIRACL Japanese slice (Apache-2.0, ungated) so the blog's\n     actual Japanese query exercises stages 1-2.\n   - Test fixtures: a small slice of REAL docs + REAL qrels committed to\n     `data/01_raw/`, licence permitting.\n\n4. **Kedro — the 8-stage query pipeline becomes a REAL Kedro pipeline**, not a\n   viz-only DAG. User reaffirmed this after being told the cost (per-query\n   session overhead, awkward for the agent's dynamic re-invocation); their\n   reason is educational value. Resolution: the 8 stages are real Kedro nodes\n   runnable via `kedro run --pipeline query` and visible in `kedro viz`; the\n   agent re-invokes those same nodes programmatically through `SequentialRunner`\n   over an in-memory catalog, so there is no duplicate implementation and no\n   disk round-trip.\n\n5. **Embedder — hash embedder REMOVED.** Real embeddings only\n   (`intfloat/multilingual-e5-small`, MIT, ungated). Consequence the user\n   accepted: slower tests, model download, harder byte-determinism.\n   Open recommendation not yet ruled on: `model2vec` static embeddings are\n   real (distilled from a real model, not a hash) and ~500x faster — a way to\n   keep tests fast without reintroducing a fake.\n\n6. **Docs enforcement — executable checker.** `make docs-check` must FAIL when:\n   a package dir lacks README.md, a README lacks a ```mermaid block, a module\n   lacks its blog-reference/Assumptions/Alternatives docstring header, or a blog\n   anchor is dead. Wired into a git pre-commit hook, `make check`, and CI.\n   Prose in AGENTS.md alone was explicitly rejected as unenforceable.\n\n7. **Learning formats — all four.** Folder READMEs with mermaid; a runnable\n   notebook per stage; a `docs/` guided learning path; and a\n   `cybernaut-mini explain --stage N` CLI inspector.\n\n8. **Commits — one per build-guide Part E milestone**, each independently green\n   (tests + lint + types + docs-check).\n\n## Baseline at time of decision\n204 tests passing, `make check` green, Kedro `index_build` + `evaluation`\npipelines exist, zero blog references anywhere in `src/`, exactly one README in","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"262919c7-4e5d-4ab7-ae30-272fbf917791","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:33:41.829Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\ntitle: \"Cybernaut-mini: scope decisions (2026-07-28)\"\ntags: [\"cybernaut\", \"planning\", \"kedro\", \"corpus\", \"docs\"]\ncreated: 2026-07-28T16:06:56.260Z\nupdated: 2026-07-28T16:06:56.260Z\nsources: []\nlinks: []\ncategory: decision\nconfidence: medium\nschemaVersion: 1\n---\n\n# Cybernaut-mini: scope decisions (2026-07-28)\n\nDecisions agreed with the user before planning the cybernaut-mini rebuild.\nReference blog: https://nosible.com/blog/the-road-to-cybernaut-1\nLocal copies: `data/00_reference/the-road-to-cybernaut-1.md` and `.build-guide.md`.\n\n## Goal\nReverse-engineer the NOSIBLE Cybernaut-1 retrieval stack as a *learning* repo.\nEvery component must carry direct blog references, stated assumptions, what the\ncode does to overcome them, and which alternatives were rejected and why.\n\n## Locked decisions\n\n1. **Layout — stage-numbered packages.** `build/` (Part A), `query/s1_language`\n   … `query/s8_retrieve` (Part B stages 1-8), `agent/` (Part C), `core/`\n   (rrf, models, config, trace). Splits the current `routing.py`, which today\n   fuses blog stages 5 AND 6 into one function.\n\n2. **Scope — all offline-capable NOT-BUILT components.** harmonic-TFIDF search\n   intents with POS filtering, instruction-template system, bloom filters,\n   trained zstd dictionaries, Aho-Corasick full-text intent pass, Bayesian dense\n   selector, Personalized PageRank reranker, prompt-injection rules,\n   multilingual stages 1-2. Neural reranker / LLM judge / LLM summaries stay\n   pluggable providers.\n\n3