{"parentUuid":"350e6e2c-f374-4367-9db0-d83867a9ed04","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpudHQ9oEnHbaaRoGgPo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":59184,"output_tokens":1068,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":59184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpudDch6K8awegBFqbyK","type":"assistant","uuid":"b52ab768-ba3a-4528-b4c0-316e9757c145","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:44:35.090Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b52ab768-ba3a-4528-b4c0-316e9757c145","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpudHQ9oEnHbaaRoGgPo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done — three changes, all in `.devcontainer/`:\n\n**`devcontainer.json:41`** — added the bind mount:\n```jsonc\n\"source=${localEnv:HOME}/.aws,target=/home/vscode/.aws,type=bind,consistency=cached\"\n```\nDeliberately **not** `readonly`, unlike the `~/env` mount. `aws sso login` and any `credential_process` write to `~/.aws/sso/cache`, and a readonly bind turns that into a permission error at login time. The cost is that the container can write to your real host credentials.\n\n**`devcontainer.json:30`** — `initializeCommand` now runs `mkdir -p \"$HOME/.aws\"` on the host first. Without it, if `~/.aws` doesn't exist on the Mac, Docker auto-creates the bind source as a **root-owned** directory, and every credential read inside the container then fails in a way that looks like \"no credentials\" rather than \"wrong permissions.\"\n\n**`Dockerfile`** — installs AWS CLI v2 from the official zip, arch-aware for amd64/aarch64, matching the existing duckdb/yq/eza blocks. Debian ships no v2 package. Binary only; no credentials in the image.\n\n**What I verified vs. didn't:** the JSONC parses and the three mounts resolve as intended. I could **not** verify it works — Docker isn't reachable from inside the container, so I can't rebuild or test the mount. That needs a **Rebuild Container** from VS Code (Cmd-Shift-P → \"Dev Containers: Rebuild Container\"). Expect a few minutes; the AWS CLI layer invalidates everything below it.\n\nAfter the rebuild:\n```\n! aws sts get-caller-identity\n```\nIf that returns an account and ARN, it's live.\n\nTwo things to be aware of. First, I couldn't confirm `~/.aws` exists on your Mac — `/run/host_mark/Users` shows in the mount table but isn't traversable from here. If it doesn't exist, the rebuild will succeed and give you an empty directory, so `get-caller-identity` will fail with \"Unable to locate credentials\" and you'd run `aws sso login` (or `aws configure`) on the host first. Second, `env/zshrc:139` forces `AWS_PROFILE=default`; once the mount is real that becomes correct only if your host profile is literally named `default`. If it's named something else, add `AWS_PROFILE=<name>` to `.env` — the `--env-file` runArg carries it in, and the zshrc line uses `${AWS_PROFILE:-default}` so it won't clobber it. There are currently no AWS entries in `.env` or `.env.example`.\n\nLeft uncommitted — say the word and I'll commit it. Note this is infrastructure only; it doesn't pull AWS into the code, so the local-first sequencing stands, and the two open questions from earlier (the gstack submodule, and components-vs-corpus ordering) are still unanswered."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":59184,"output_tokens":1068,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":59184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpudDch6K8awegBFqbyK","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f7e3289-7896-4930-b7b0-1d2c051caa50","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:44:46.592Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
