{"parentUuid":"c05669a4-44bb-4dca-867a-4ef566256799","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FmMJrojK2Vy8DBpqsWA92Z","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"continue\":true,\"suppressOutput\":true}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\"/scripts/run.cjs \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\"/scripts/pre-tool-enforcer.mjs","durationMs":78},"type":"attachment","uuid":"751d8e86-a341-480e-a59a-1cf6b49a6d91","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:47:42.628Z","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c05669a4-44bb-4dca-867a-4ef566256799","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"308afc9b-6e5b-47dc-a4a5-b09e9ddfddf6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FmMJrojK2Vy8DBpqsWA92Z","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntitle: \"Nosible Hugging Face Artifacts: Models & Datasets\"\ntags: [\"nosible\", \"huggingface\", \"models\", \"datasets\", \"qwen3\", \"distillation\", \"financial-sentiment\", \"forward-looking\", \"prediction\", \"active-learning\", \"odc-by\"]\ncreated: 2026-07-29T17:21:00.361Z\nupdated: 2026-07-29T17:21:00.361Z\nsources: [\"docs/huggingface-archive/\"]\nlinks: [\"docs-archive-overview.md\", \"nosible-blog-archive-research-engineering-digest.md\", \"nosible-py-official-nosible-search-api-client.md\", \"smol-html-html-cleaner-minifier-for-web-scale-ingest.md\"]\ncategory: reference\nconfidence: high\nschemaVersion: 1\n---\n\n# Nosible Hugging Face Artifacts: Models & Datasets\n\n# Nosible Hugging Face Artifacts: Models & Datasets\n\n> Digest of `docs/huggingface-archive/` (ingested 2026-07-29). Related: [[docs-archive-overview]], [[nosible-blog-archive-research-engineering-digest]], [[nosible-py-official-nosible-search-api-client]], [[smol-html-html-cleaner-minifier-for-web-scale-ingest]].\n\nThe one layer of the NOSIBLE stack needing **no reverse-engineering** — weights and 300k labelled rows are downloadable. Guide §3's output.\n\n## Models (5 repos, all Apache-2.0)\n\nAll are 596M-param `qwen3` causal LMs fine-tuned from `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-Base`, run as **constrained single-token classifiers**. v1.1 released 2025-11-25 (served live by featherless-ai); v1.2 released 2026-04-28 (weights only). No `prediction-v1.2`.\n\n| Model | Task | Labels | Downloads |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `financial-sentiment-v1.2-base` | valence (financial impact) | positive / neutral / negative | 2.9K |\n| `financial-sentiment-v1.1-base` | valence | same | 4.5K |\n| `forward-looking-v1.2-base` | tense | `forward` / `not forward` (space!) | 2.8K |\n| `forward-looking-v1.1-base` | tense | same | 724 |\n| `prediction-v1.1-base` | modality | `prediction` / `not-prediction` (hyphen!) | 365 |\n\n### Three mandatory usage requirements (per card)\n1. `enable_thinking=False` — fine-tuned to emit exactly one label token.\n2. **Exact system prompt verbatim** (e.g. `Classify the financial sentiment as positive, neutral, or negative.`) — present on every training example; it's a task key, not a description.\n3. **Constrain output** to the label set via regex/grammar/guided decoding. Recommended serving: SGLang (`python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path NOSIBLE/financial-sentiment-v1.2-base`).\n\n⚠️ Label-string inconsistency across the family (`not forward` vs `not-prediction`) — build decoding grammars per checkpoint. Also: `prediction-v1.1` card points at `NOSIBLE/predictive` (not public); assume it's `NOSIBLE/prediction` renamed.\n\n### Benchmarks & training\n- financial-sentiment v1.1: 87.70% English; beats FinBERT's 86% on Financial PhraseBank (held out entirely from training). v1.2: English flat (87.97%) but multilingual 76.69%→83.16% and currency/geo feeds 67.30%→76.17% — 94 languages; multilingual is the whole story.\n- Disclosed training config (family spec): lr 2e-5, cosine + 0.03 warmup, batch 64, **2 epochs** (deliberate under-training on noisy committee labels), AdamW fused, bf16, **NEFTune α=5**, weight decay 0.1, max len 2048, loss masked to the single assistant label token (`labels=-100` elsewhere).\n- Limitations: finance-only, no aspect/entity binding (event layer's job — guide §8), 2048-token context, per-language variance.\n\n## Datasets (3 repos, ODC-By v1.0, 100,000 rows each)\n\nReleased 2025-11-26, v1.0.0. Shared schema: `text`, `label`, `netloc`, `url`; single `train` split; English; Parquet. Sourced from **NOSIBLE Search Feeds** on finance queries — already cleaned (smol-html), deduplicated (event layer), on-topic chunks (128–1024-token `n_contextify` window), *not* a random web sample.\n\n| Dataset | Labels | Downloads |\n|---|---|---|\n| `financial-sentiment` | positive / neutral / negative — by **potential financial impact**, not tone | 73 |\n| `forward-looking` | forward / not forward | 26 |\n| `prediction` | prediction / not-prediction | 23 |\n\n### Shared annotation pipeline (disclosed, = guide §3)\n1. Hand-label ~200 samples for prompt tuning.\n2. Label 100k rows with **8 LLM annotators** (Grok 4, Gemini 2.5, GPT variants incl. GPT-5, Llama 4, Qwen3).\n3. Train **linear ensemble models over 6 embedding models** — cheap consistent probe whose disagreement with the committee is a free active-learning acquisition function.\n4. **GPT-5.1 oracle** adjudicates disagreements iteratively.\n5. **Drop** underperforming annotators (pruned, not down-weighted); repeat to convergence.\n\nConsequences: labels are model-derived consensus (shared blind spots included); no published class balance, agreement stats, or eval split — the external PhraseBank benchmark carries the evidential weight.\n\n## The orthogonal-axes design\n\n| Axis | Question | Model |\n|---|---|---|\n| Valence | Good or bad financial impact? | financial-sentiment |\n| Tense | About the future? | forward-looking |\n| Modality | Forecast, or report? | prediction |\n\n\"We will open 40 stores next year\" = forward but **not** a prediction (commitment); \"In hindsight, we had forecast a downturn\" = not forward but **is** a prediction. Crossing the three separates guidance-from-results and issuer-intent from third-party estimates. The missing axis — *which entity* — is deliberately absent; entity binding happens in the event layer.\n\n## For cybernaut_mini\n\n- Repo mapping: committee → `providers/judge.py`; linear probe → `providers/embeddings.py`; disagreement/oracle loop → `evals.py`; corpus loading → `datasets.py`; distil target → `models.py`.\n- **Split by `netloc`, not by row** — random splits leak syndicated wire copy.\n- Start the distil loop on `forward-looking` (binary, cleaner agreement stats), then port to 3-class sentiment. `prediction` is the stalest head (no v1.2, name mismatch, fewest downloads) — use compositionally, not as a target.\n- **ODC-By attribution required** for any public use: Matthew Dicks, Simon van Dyk, Stuart Reid; NOSIBLE Inc.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"96ede8b6-613b-4ce1-9fca-cbb7b90d246f","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:47:42.744Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\ntitle: \"Nosible Hugging Face Artifacts: Models & Datasets\"\ntags: [\"nosible\", \"huggingface\", \"models\", \"datasets\", \"qwen3\", \"distillation\", \"financial-sentiment\", \"forward-looking\", \"prediction\", \"active-learning\", \"odc-by\"]\ncreated: 2026-07-29T17:21:00.361Z\nupdated: 2026-07-29T17:21:00.361Z\nsources: [\"docs/huggingface-archive/\"]\nlinks: [\"docs-archive-overview.md\", \"nosible-blog-archive-research-engineering-digest.md\", \"nosible-py-official-nosible-search-api-client.md\", \"smol-html-html-cleaner-minifier-for-web-scale-ingest.md\"]\ncategory: reference\nconfidence: high\nschemaVersion: 1\n---\n\n# Nosible Hugging Face Artifacts: Models & Datasets\n\n# Nosible Hugging Face Artifacts: Models & Datasets\n\n> Digest of `docs/huggingface-archive/` (ingested 2026-07-29). Related: [[docs-archive-overview]], [[nosible-blog-archive-research-engineering-digest]], [[nosible-py-official-nosible-search-api-client]], [[smol-html-html-cleaner-minifier-for-web-scale-ingest]].\n\nThe one layer of the NOSIBLE stack needing **no reverse-engineering** — weights and 300k labelled rows are downloadable. Guide §3's output.\n\n## Models (5 repos, all Apache-2.0)\n\nAll are 596M-param `qwen3` causal LMs fine-tuned from `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-Base`, run as **constrained single-token classifiers**. v1.1 released 2025-11-25 (served live by featherless-ai); v1.2 released 2026-04-28 (weights only). No `prediction-v1.2`.\n\n| Model | Task | Labels | Downloads |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `financial-sentiment-v1.2-base` | valence (financial impact) | positive / neutral / negative | 2.9K |\n| `financial-sentiment-v1.1-base` | valence | same | 4.5K |\n| `forward-looking-v1.2-base` | tense | `forward` / `not forward` (space!) | 2.8K |\n| `forward-looking-v1.1-base` | tense | same | 724 |\n| `prediction-v1.1-base` | modality | `prediction` / `not-prediction` (hyphen!) | 365 |\n\n### Three mandatory usage requirements (per card)\n1. `enable_thinking=False` — fine-tuned to emit exactly one label token.\n2. **Exact system prompt verbatim** (e.g. `Classify the financial sentiment as positive, neutral, or negative.`) — present on every training example; it's a task key, not a description.\n3. **Constrain output** to the label set via regex/grammar/guided decoding. Recommended serving: SGLang (`python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path NOSIBLE/financial-sentiment-v1.2-base`).\n\n⚠️ Label-string inconsistency across the family (`not forward` vs `not-prediction`) — build decoding grammars per checkpoint. Also: `prediction-v1.1` card points at `NOSIBLE/predictive` (not public); assume it's `NOSIBLE/prediction` renamed.\n\n### Benchmarks & training\n- financial-sentiment v1.1: 87.70% English; beats FinBERT's 86% on Financial PhraseBank (held out entirely from training). v1.2: English flat (87.97%) but multilingual 76.69%→83.16% and currency/geo feeds 67.30%→76.17% — 94 languages; multilingual is the whole story.\n- Disclosed training config (family spec): lr 2e-5, cosine + 0.03 warmup, batch 64, **2 epochs** (deliberate under-training on noisy committee labels), AdamW fused, bf16, **NEFTune α=5**, weight decay 0.1, max len 2048, loss masked to the single assistant label token (`labels=-100` elsewhere).\n- Limitations: finance-only, no aspect/entity binding (event layer's job — guide §8), 2048-token context, per-language variance.\n\n## Datasets (3 repos, ODC-By v1.0, 100,000 rows each)\n\nReleased 2025-11-26, v1.0.0. Shared schema: `text`, `label`, `netloc`, `url`; single `train` split; English; Parquet. Sourced from **NOSIBLE Search Feeds** on finance queries — already cleaned (smol-html), deduplicated (event layer), on-topic chunks (128–1024-token `n_contextify` window), *not* a random web sample.\n\n| Dataset | Labels | Downloads |\n|---|---|---|\n| `financial-sentiment` | positive / neutral / negative — by **potential financial impact**, not tone | 73 |\n| `forward-looking` | forward / not forward | 26 |\n| `prediction` | prediction / not-prediction | 23 |\n\n### Shared annotation pipeline (disclosed, = guide §3)\n1. Hand-label ~200 samples for prompt tuning.\n2. Label 100k rows with **8 LLM annotators** (Grok 4, Gemini 2.5, GPT variants incl. GPT-5, Llama 4, Qwen3).\n3. Train **linear ensemble models over 6 embedding models** — cheap consistent probe whose disagreement with the committee is a free active-learning acquisition function.\n4. **GPT-5.1 oracle** adjudicates disagreements iteratively.\n5. **Drop** underperforming annotators (pruned, not down-weighted); repeat to convergence.\n\nConsequences: labels are model-derived consensus (shared blind spots included); no published class balance, agreement stats, or eval split — the external PhraseBank benchmark carries the evidential weight.\n\n## The orthogonal-axes design\n\n| Axis | Question | Model |\n|---|---|---|\n| Valence | Good or bad financial impact? | financial-sentiment |\n| Tense | About the future? | forward-looking |\n| Modality | Forecast, or report? | prediction |\n\n\"We will open 40 stores next year\" = forward but **not** a prediction (commitment); \"In hindsight, we had forecast a downturn\" = not forward but **is** a prediction. Crossing the three separates guidance-from-results and issuer-intent from third-party estimates. The missing axis — *which entity* — is deliberately absent; entity binding happens in the event layer.\n\n## For cybernaut_mini\n\n- Repo mapping: committee → `providers/judge.py`; linear probe → `providers/embeddings.py`; disagreement/oracle loop → `evals.py`; corpus loading → `datasets.py`; distil 