{"parentUuid":"51881b11-ff8c-43ae-906a-82ad77a539f2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"308afc9b-6e5b-47dc-a4a5-b09e9ddfddf6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ALQwHRYj8L7G1qgHuXo1o","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspaces/cybernaut_mini/.omc/wiki/cybernaut-mini-scope-decisions-2026-07-28.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"143c4674-d78e-4cfc-a398-4295297a8aae","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:51:58.969Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini/.omc/wiki/cybernaut-mini-scope-decisions-2026-07-28.md","oldString":"5. **The learning mandate is unchanged and still primary.** User reaffirmed:\n   \"I still need to understand the tech.\" Decisions 6 and 7 above (executable\n   `make docs-check`, folder READMEs with mermaid, per-stage notebooks, guided\n   `docs/` path, `explain --stage N`) apply to every component added under the\n   new fidelity goal — wider reproduction means more to document, not less.","newString":"5. **The learning mandate is unchanged and still primary.** User reaffirmed:\n   \"I still need to understand the tech.\" Decisions 6 and 7 above (executable\n   `make docs-check`, folder READMEs with mermaid, per-stage notebooks, guided\n   `docs/` path, `explain --stage N`) apply to every component added under the\n   new fidelity goal — wider reproduction means more to document, not less.\n\n6. **Decision 3 (corpus) SUPERSEDED — FineWeb-2 spine + MIRACL evals.**\n\n   *Why SciFact had to go:* it is ~5.2k documents, which is roughly ONE shard.\n   Blog stages 5-7 (shard selection, shard reranking, shard-based question\n   expansion) exist only because 250,000 shards do, and the blog calls shard\n   selection \"arguably the single most important stage in our retrieval\n   pipeline.\" At SciFact scale those three stages cannot be exercised at all.\n   The corpus had to grow for *fidelity* reasons, not scale-for-its-own-sake.\n\n   - **Bulk corpus: `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2`** (ODC-By, 1000+ languages).\n     Cleaned CommonCrawl — the same class of input NOSIBLE ingests, and it\n     carries the Japanese needed for the blog's bilingual gene-editing example.\n   - **Eval substrate: `miracl/miracl-corpus` + MIRACL qrels** (Apache-2.0,\n     16 languages incl. `ja`, expert-generated judgments).\n   - **NOT a corpus: the three NOSIBLE HF datasets.** `financial-sentiment`,\n     `forward-looking`, `prediction` are 100k-row *classification* sets\n     (`text`/`label`/`netloc`/`url`) with no queries, qrels, or doc IDs. They\n     feed the classifier heads (guide §3) only. Verified live 2026-08-08: the\n     NOSIBLE org is 8 repos, unchanged since Dec 2025, and publishes no\n     retrieval corpus. See [[nosible-hugging-face-artifacts-models-datasets]].\n   - **Rejected:** MS MARCO (research-only licence); raw CommonCrawl + smol-html\n     (maximum fidelity but heavy bandwidth/CPU and zero qrels) — reconsider once\n     the AWS phase starts.\n   - **Attribution owed:** ODC-By for FineWeb-2 and the NOSIBLE datasets\n     (Matthew Dicks, Simon van Dyk, Stuart Reid; NOSIBLE Inc.).\n\n7. **Eval policy — dual-track, never conflated.** Two separate namespaces:\n   - *Real qrels* (MIRACL/BEIR) are the trusted benchmark. Any reported quality\n     number comes from here.\n   - *Generated per-shard evals* reproduce blog line 61 (\"Evals — Gold standard\n     datasets for evaluating this shard\"), which NOSIBLE genuinely does. Queries\n     are LLM-generated; **documents are always real**. This does not violate the\n     no-dummy-data rule — the rule bans fabricated documents and fabricated\n     judgments over fabricated documents, and this is neither.\n   - The two must never be averaged, merged, or reported as one figure.\n\n## Open questions (as of 2026-08-08)\n\n- **Target machine unknown.** \"Single big machine\" is undefined. The dev\n  container has 7.7 GiB RAM / 8 cores / 355G disk, which caps out around 1-2M\n  documents with int8-quantised embeddings — far short of the ≥200 shards\n  needed to make shard selection a real decision (~1M-30M docs).\n- **Shard-size assumption unresolved.** The blog is internally inconsistent:\n  \"almost a billion webpages\" over 250,000 shards implies ~4,000 docs/shard,\n  but the worked example (shard 11,343) reports 134,523 documents — a 34× gap.\n  Either the shard count is aspirational or \"documents\" are chunks, not pages.\n  Pick one, document it in the module Assumptions header.\n- **`e149331` (gstack submodule)** — committed as \"a deliberate step off the\n  nosible stack\", the framing now dropped. Park or keep? Unresolved.\n- **Sequencing** — NOT-BUILT components first, or corpus scale-up first?\n  Standing recommendation: components first; scaling an incomplete stack means\n  scaling it twice.","originalFile":"---\ntitle: \"Cybernaut-mini: scope decisions (2026-07-28)\"\ntags: [\"cybernaut\", \"planning\", \"kedro\", \"corpus\", \"docs\"]\ncreated: 2026-07-28T16:06:56.260Z\nupdated: 2026-07-28T16:06:56.260Z\nsources: []\nlinks: []\ncategory: decision\nconfidence: medium\nschemaVersion: 1\n---\n\n# Cybernaut-mini: scope decisions (2026-07-28)\n\nDecisions agreed with the user before planning the cybernaut-mini rebuild.\nReference blog: https://nosible.com/blog/the-road-to-cybernaut-1\nLocal copies: `data/00_reference/the-road-to-cybernaut-1.md` and `.build-guide.md`.\n\n## Goal\nReverse-engineer the NOSIBLE Cybernaut-1 retrieval stack as a *learning* repo.\nEvery component must carry direct blog references, stated assumptions, what the\ncode does to overcome them, and which alternatives were rejected and why.\n\n## Locked decisions\n\n1. **Layout — stage-numbered packages.** `build/` (Part A), `query/s1_language`\n   … `query/s8_retrieve` (Part B stages 1-8), `agent/` (Part C), `core/`\n   (rrf, models, config, trace). Splits the current `routing.py`, which today\n   fuses blog stages 5 AND 6 into one function.\n\n2. **Scope — all offline-capable NOT-BUILT components.** harmonic-TFIDF search\n   intents with POS filtering, instruction-template system, bloom filters,\n   trained zstd dictionaries, Aho-Corasick full-text intent pass, Bayesian dense\n   selector, Personalized PageRank reranker, prompt-injection rules,\n   multilingual stages 1-2. Neural reranker / LLM judge / LLM summaries stay\n   pluggable providers.\n\n3. **Corpus — REAL DATA ONLY. User was emphatic: \"THIS MUST NEVER USE DUMMY\n   DATA.\"** The existing 63-doc synthetic corpus and its fabricated judgments\n   are to be removed.\n   - Primary: BEIR SciFact (~5.2k real PubMed abstracts, real qrels,\n     CC BY-SA 4.0 as `BeIR/scifact`; note original `allenai/scifact` is tagged\n     CC BY-NC 2.0 — data needs its own attribution/licence file, not MIT).\n   - Multilingual: MIRACL Japanese slice (Apache-2.0, ungated) so the blog's\n     actual Japanese query exercises stages 1-2.\n   - Test fixtures: a small slice of REAL docs + REAL qrels committed to\n     `data/01_raw/`, licence permitting.\n\n4. **Kedro — the 8-stage query pipeline becomes a REAL Kedro pipeline**, not a\n   viz-only DAG. User reaffirmed this after being told the cost (per-query\n   session overhead, awkward for the agent's dynamic re-invocation); their\n   reason is educational value. Resolution: the 8 stages are real Kedro nodes\n   runnable via `kedro run --pipeline query` and visible in `kedro viz`; the\n   agent re-invokes those same nodes programmatically through `SequentialRunner`\n   over an in-memory catalog, so there is no duplicate implementation and no\n   disk round-trip.\n\n5. **Embedder — hash embedder REMOVED.** Real embeddings only\n   (`intfloat/multilingual-e5-small`, MIT, ungated). Consequence the user\n   accepted: slower tests, model download, harder byte-determinism.\n   Open recommendation not yet ruled on: `model2vec` static embeddings are\n   real (distilled from a real model, not a hash) and ~500x faster — a way to\n   keep tests fast without reintroducing a fake.\n\n6. **Docs enforcement — executable checker.** `make docs-check` must FAIL when:\n   a package dir lacks README.md, a README lacks a ```mermaid block, a module\n   lacks its blog-reference/Assumptions/Alternatives docstring header, or a blog\n   anchor is dead. Wired into a git pre-commit hook, `make check`, and CI.\n   Prose in AGENTS.md alone was explicitly rejected as unenforceable.\n\n7. **Learning formats — all four.** Folder READMEs with mermaid; a runnable\n   notebook per stage; a `docs/` guided learning path; and a\n   `cybernaut-mini explain --stage N` CLI inspector.\n\n8. **Commits — one per build-guide Part E milestone**, each independently green\n   (tests + lint + types + docs-check).\n\n## Baseline at time of decision\n204 tests passing, `make check` green, Kedro `index_build` + `evaluation`\npipelines exist, zero blog references anywhere in `src/`, exactly one README in\nthe repo.\n\n## Amendment 2026-08-08 — differentiation dropped, fidelity + scale adopted\n\nReverses the short-lived \"build a shard NOSIBLE does not carry\" direction.\n\n1. **AIS trade-flow shard parked, not deleted.** Commit `4531e4f` (`trade.py`,\n   `pipelines/trade_ingest/`, its catalog + parameters entries, `test_trade.py`;\n   548 lines) was the unpushed tip of `main`. Preserved intact on branch\n   `shard/ais-trade-flow`; `main` rewound to `e149331`. Recoverable at any time.\n   Orphaned pipeline outputs `data/01_raw/ais_snapshot.jsonl` and\n   `data/02_intermediate/ais_positions.jsonl` deliberately left on disk.\n\n2. **New goal — reproduce the NOSIBLE stack as closely as possible, at scale.**\n   Novel components are out of scope; fidelity to the blog is the objective.\n\n3. **Scale target — full corpus on a single large host.** Not a distributed\n   cloud build. Corpus and index grow to NOSIBLE-like volume while staying\n   runnable on one machine.\n\n4. **AWS is a later phase, explicitly deferred.** \"Move to AWS after we do as\n   much locally as we can.\" No cloud dependency may be introduced before that\n   phase. Note: no AWS credentials exist in the devcontainer — `~/.aws` is\n   absent, no key env vars, no `aws` CLI, and `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`\n   binds only `~/env` and `~/.ssh`. The `AWS_PROFILE=default` seen in-container\n   is a false signal set unconditionally by `env/zshrc:139`.\n\n5. **The learning mandate is unchanged and still primary.** User reaffirmed:\n   \"I still need to understand the tech.\" Decisions 6 and 7 above (executable\n   `make docs-check`, folder READMEs with mermaid, per-stage notebooks, guided\n   `docs/` path, `explain --stage N`) apply to every component added under the\n   new fidelity goal — wider reproduction means more to document, not less.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":111,"oldLines":3,"newStart":111,"newLines":56,"lines":["    `docs/` path, `explain --stage N`) apply to every component added under the","    new fidelity goal — wider reproduction means more to document, not less."," ","+6. **Decision 3 (corpus) SUPERSEDED — FineWeb-2 spine + MIRACL evals.**","+","+   *Why SciFact had to go:* it is ~5.2k documents, which is roughly ONE shard.","+   Blog stages 5-7 (shard selection, shard reranking, shard-based question","+   expansion) exist only because 250,000 shards do, and the blog calls shard","+   selection \"arguably the single most important stage in our retrieval","+   pipeline.\" At SciFact scale those three stages cannot be exercised at all.","+   The corpus had to grow for *fidelity* reasons, not scale-for-its-own-sake.","+","+   - **Bulk corpus: `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2`** (ODC-By, 1000+ languages).","+     Cleaned CommonCrawl — the same class of input NOSIBLE ingests, and it","+     carries the Japanese needed for the blog's bilingual gene-editing example.","+   - **Eval substrate: `miracl/miracl-corpus` + MIRACL qrels** (Apache-2.0,","+     16 languages incl. `ja`, expert-generated judgments).","+   - **NOT a corpus: the three NOSIBLE HF datasets.** `financial-sentiment`,","+     `forward-looking`, `prediction` are 100k-row *classification* sets","+     (`text`/`label`/`netloc`/`url`) with no queries, qrels, or doc IDs. They","+     feed the classifier heads (guide §3) only. Verified live 2026-08-08: the","+     NOSIBLE org is 8 repos, unchanged since Dec 2025, and publishes no","+     retrieval corpus. See [[nosible-hugging-face-artifacts-models-datasets]].","+   - **Rejected:** MS MARCO (research-only licence); raw CommonCrawl + smol-html","+     (maximum fidelity but heavy bandwidth/CPU and zero qrels) — reconsider once","+     the AWS phase starts.","+   - **Attribution owed:** ODC-By for FineWeb-2 and the NOSIBLE datasets","+     (Matthew Dicks, Simon van Dyk, Stuart Reid; NOSIBLE Inc.).","+","+7. **Eval policy — dual-track, never conflated.** Two separate namespaces:","+   - *Real qrels* (MIRACL/BEIR) are the trusted benchmark. Any reported quality","+     number comes from here.","+   - *Generated per-shard evals* reproduce blog line 61 (\"Evals — Gold standard","+     datasets for evaluating this shard\"), which NOSIBLE genuinely does. Queries","+     are LLM-generated; **documents are always real**. This does not violate the","+     no-dummy-data rule — the rule bans fabricated documents and fabricated","+     judgments over fabricated documents, and this is neither.","+   - The two must never be averaged, merged, or reported as one figure.","+","+## Open questions (as of 2026-08-08)","+","+- **Target machine unknown.** \"Single big machine\" is undefined. The dev","+  container has 7.7 GiB RAM / 8 cores / 355G disk, which caps out around 1-2M","+  documents with int8-quantised embeddings — far short of the ≥200 shards","+  needed to make shard selection a real decision (~1M-30M docs).","+- **Shard-size assumption unresolved.** The blog is internally inconsistent:","+  \"almost a billion webpages\" over 250,000 shards implies ~4,000 docs/shard,","+  but the worked example (shard 11,343) reports 134,523 documents — a 34× gap.","+  Either the shard count is aspirational or \"documents\" are chunks, not pages.","+  Pick one, document it in the module Assumptions header.","+- **`e149331` (gstack submodule)** — committed as \"a deliberate step off the","+  nosible stack\", the framing now dropped. Park or keep? Unresolved.","+- **Sequencing** — NOT-BUILT components first, or corpus scale-up first?","+  Standing recommendation: components first; scaling an incomplete stack means","+  scaling it twice.","+"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51881b11-ff8c-43ae-906a-82ad77a539f2","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
