{"parentUuid":"b39624b7-a2bf-4a74-a0bc-3245293d2b12","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01TZ4NQ3KntjfDwJnSqDFCmk","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"continue\":true,\"suppressOutput\":true}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\"/scripts/run.cjs \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\"/scripts/project-memory-posttool.mjs","durationMs":71},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a459436f-e731-4ac5-bbe8-2f2d594418b6","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:52:09.711Z","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a459436f-e731-4ac5-bbe8-2f2d594418b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvD4JJcyj2Kpd9TYACS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Locked in and recorded:**\n\n- **Bulk corpus** — `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2` (ODC-By, 1000+ languages, cleaned CommonCrawl)\n- **Eval substrate** — `miracl/miracl-corpus` + MIRACL qrels (Apache-2.0, expert judgments, includes `ja`)\n- **SciFact** — superseded, with the reason written down: at ~5.2k docs it's one shard, so blog stages 5–7 are untestable\n- **NOSIBLE's HF datasets** — correctly scoped to the classifier heads, not retrieval\n- **Evals** — dual-track in separate namespaces; real qrels are the only source of reported quality numbers, generated per-shard evals reproduce blog line 61 over real documents and are never averaged in\n\nOn the no-dummy-data rule: I wrote the reasoning into the record rather than leaving it implicit, because generated per-shard evals sit close to the line. The rule bans fabricated documents and fabricated judgments over fabricated documents. Generated queries over real FineWeb-2 documents is neither — and it's what NOSIBLE actually does, so omitting it would be an *infidelity*. If you read your original rule more strictly than that, say so and I'll drop the second track.\n\n**The one thing genuinely blocking scale work is still unanswered: what machine?** This container is 7.7 GiB RAM / 8 cores, which tops out near 1–2M documents even with int8 quantisation — below the ~200-shard threshold where shard selection becomes a real decision. Whether we target 1M, 10M, or 30M documents changes the ingest design, the embedding storage format, and whether HNSW stays in memory. Specs of the box, please, and whether it's this Mac or something else.\n\nAlso parked in the record as open: the blog's 34× shard-size inconsistency (4k vs 134k docs/shard — needs an assumption picked and documented), plus the two earlier items (`e149331`, and components-vs-corpus ordering). No action needed on those to answer the machine question."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":753,"cache_read_input_tokens":107771,"output_tokens":693,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":753,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":107771,"cache_creation_input_tokens":753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":753},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvD1baXnKe66APUtcBB","type":"assistant","uuid":"50a5435e-6fb6-4c38-ad5b-6de5852b3791","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:52:22.697Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
