{"parentUuid":"10ff85c8-9a80-4bec-80bb-3cafdc1f7491","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvRTvhY8Lo1dzKckBna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7519,"cache_read_input_tokens":125104,"output_tokens":3815,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3815,"cache_read_input_tokens":125104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7519},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvRST9AiFAn4GL7YCvu","attributionSkill":"mcp__exa__web_search_help","attributionMcpServer":"exa","attributionMcpTool":"web_search_exa","type":"assistant","uuid":"eaea88b7-30bc-4a9c-9bb9-fac5020c3687","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:55:18.207Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"eaea88b7-30bc-4a9c-9bb9-fac5020c3687","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvRTvhY8Lo1dzKckBna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-check is in, and it corrects my scale estimate materially.\n\n**Confirmed, and stronger than I put it:** NOSIBLE's copyright page states outright — *\"NOSIBLE is a search and retrieval product, not a bulk web corpus for redistribution.\"* They also describe open-sourcing *models*, not corpora. So the absence of a retrieval corpus is a deliberate legal posture, not a gap that might close.\n\n**Corrected — the shard ratio.** A primary source I hadn't seen, [Can Faceted Search at Web-Scale Self Organize?](https://nosible.com/research/can-faceted-search-at-web-scale-self-organize), states: *\"Our last run learned 250,000 collections from 250,000,000 documents.\"* That's **1,000 documents per collection** — a far better anchor than anything in the Cybernaut blog. My earlier \"1M–30M documents to reach ≥200 shards\" was too pessimistic:\n\n| Shards | Docs @ 1,000/shard | Feasible here? |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | 200,000 | Yes, comfortably |\n| 1,000 | 1,000,000 | Yes, with int8 |\n| 250,000 (full) | 250,000,000 | No |\n\n**A few hundred thousand documents is enough to make shard selection a real decision.** That fits the current 7.7 GiB container, so the machine question stops being a blocker for starting.\n\nThe 134,523-document figure for shard 11,343 is still the outlier — 134× the training ratio, and inconsistent with ~1B pages ÷ 250k shards ≈ 4,000. Design toward 1,000–4,000; treat 134k as unexplained rather than resolved.\n\n**Three new facts that change the build**, all from the same research page:\n\n- **Aho-Corasick is confirmed in production** for per-collection entity tagging — that NOT-BUILT item is real, not inferred\n- **Collections are flushed to disk on write and cached in RAM by size/importance** — that is precisely the single-machine architecture we need, straight from the source\n- Ingest runs 15–20M pages/day → 91M paragraphs, i.e. **~6 chunks per page** for sizing math\n- The ranker is `hybrid-3`; exposed algorithms are `lexical, baseline, hamming, hybrid-1/2/3, company` — a concrete list for `query/` to mirror, and `hamming` corroborates their LSH heritage\n\n**One thing I could not verify:** the 2025-08-26 Cybernaut-1 post promised *\"next week, we will be open-sourcing a comprehensive set of evaluations.\"* I found no such release — not on the NosibleAI GitHub, not elsewhere. Absence of evidence rather than proof, but it means there's no NOSIBLE-published qrels to lean on, so the dual-track eval decision you made stands unchanged."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7519,"cache_read_input_tokens":125104,"output_tokens":3815,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3815,"cache_read_input_tokens":125104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7519},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvRST9AiFAn4GL7YCvu","attributionSkill":"mcp__exa__web_search_help","attributionMcpServer":"exa","attributionMcpTool":"web_search_exa","type":"assistant","uuid":"8b5564fd-5b2e-46bf-bb84-d3db1325fb20","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:55:29.635Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8b5564fd-5b2e-46bf-bb84-d3db1325fb20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvRTvhY8Lo1dzKckBna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wj2wn1wWYPo7kccdR5mFb4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini/.omc/wiki/cybernaut-mini-scope-decisions-2026-07-28.md","old_string":"- **Target machine unknown.** \"Single big machine\" is undefined. The dev\n  container has 7.7 GiB RAM / 8 cores / 355G disk, which caps out around 1-2M\n  documents with int8-quantised embeddings — far short of the ≥200 shards\n  needed to make shard selection a real decision (~1M-30M docs).\n- **Shard-size assumption unresolved.** The blog is internally inconsistent:\n  \"almost a billion webpages\" over 250,000 shards implies ~4,000 docs/shard,\n  but the worked example (shard 11,343) reports 134,523 documents — a 34× gap.\n  Either the shard count is aspirational or \"documents\" are chunks, not pages.\n  Pick one, document it in the module Assumptions header.","new_string":"- **Shard-size assumption — RESOLVED ENOUGH TO BUILD (web cross-check\n  2026-08-08).** `nosible.com/research/can-faceted-search-at-web-scale-self-organize`\n  (mirror `nosible.ghost.io`, 2025-10-16) states: \"Our last run learned 250,000\n  collections from 250,000,000 documents\" = **1,000 documents per collection**.\n  This supersedes the earlier guess. Three ratios now exist:\n  | Source | Ratio | Status |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Research page, actual training run | 1,000 docs/shard | **Use this** |\n  | ~1B pages ÷ 250k shards (blog) | ~4,000 pages/shard | Plausible upper bound |\n  | Shard 11,343 worked example (blog) | 134,523 docs | Unexplained outlier |\n  Design toward **1,000-4,000 docs/shard**; record 134,523 as unexplained in the\n  module Assumptions header rather than pretending it reconciles.\n\n- **Scale target REVISED DOWN — the machine is no longer a blocker.** At 1,000\n  docs/shard, 200 shards ≈ 200k documents and 1,000 shards ≈ 1M documents. Both\n  fit the existing 7.7 GiB / 8-core container with int8-quantised embeddings.\n  The earlier \"1M-30M documents\" estimate was derived from the outlier ratio and\n  was too pessimistic. Work can start now; the big-machine question only returns\n  when we push past ~1M docs.\n\n- **Single-machine architecture is disclosed, not guesswork.** Same research\n  page: collections are written to on ingest, \"every so often those writes are\n  flushed to disk\", and \"larger or most important collections are flushed more\n  frequently and are also more likely to be cached in RAM.\" That is exactly the\n  RAM/disk tiering a single-host build needs — copy it rather than invent one.\n\n- **Cross-check corroborations (2026-08-08):**\n  - **Aho-Corasick is in production**, as a per-collection non-neural entity\n    tagger fed by a slow universal neural tagger + a Resolver Agent. The\n    NOT-BUILT list item is real, not inferred.\n  - Ingest is 15-20M pages/day → 91M paragraphs/day, i.e. **~6 chunks/page**.\n  - Ranker is `hybrid-3`; exposed algorithms are `lexical, baseline, hamming,\n    hybrid-1/2/3, company`. `hamming` corroborates the LSH heritage described\n    in the 2024 \"Using Vector Search to See Signals in Company News\" post.\n  - **NOSIBLE will never publish a retrieval corpus.** `nosible.com/legal/copyright`:\n    \"NOSIBLE is a search and retrieval product, not a bulk web corpus for\n    redistribution.\" A legal posture, not an oversight. Confirms the FineWeb-2\n    decision is the only path.\n  - **Promised open evals NOT FOUND.** The 2025-08-26 Cybernaut-1 post said\n    \"next week, we will be open-sourcing a comprehensive set of evaluations\"\n    (Cybernaut-1 and Hybrid-3 vs leading search engines). No such release found\n    on NosibleAI GitHub or elsewhere as of 2026-08-08. Absence of evidence, not\n    proof of absence — but there is no NOSIBLE-published qrels to rely on, so\n    amendment 7's dual-track eval policy stands.\n\n- **Target machine still unstated** — only matters past ~1M documents now."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7519,"cache_read_input_tokens":125104,"output_tokens":3815,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3815,"cache_read_input_tokens":125104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7519},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvRST9AiFAn4GL7YCvu","attributionSkill":"mcp__exa__web_search_help","attributionMcpServer":"exa","attributionMcpTool":"web_search_exa","type":"assistant","uuid":"7046ce43-4ffd-4094-b986-6b4c15cf423d","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:55:46.855Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
