{"parentUuid":"5dfadec3-c8f7-4fc3-b1c8-8a38d408eff3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvksdVgde6e65uB8fdz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":147365,"output_tokens":4064,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4064,"cache_read_input_tokens":147365,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvkrHtDLmaU1eTSDkzD","type":"assistant","uuid":"80caa8ff-18f8-4907-8d41-d3bf364ad7ac","timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:59:52.759Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"80caa8ff-18f8-4907-8d41-d3bf364ad7ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvksdVgde6e65uB8fdz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two things verified that make this concrete. (I read only the schema section of that 6,442-line FineWeb-2 config dump, not the full per-language listing — the field list is what mattered.)\n\n**FineWeb-2 carries `url`, `date`, `language`, `language_score`, `minhash_cluster_size`.** So it can be filtered by domain and ordered in time.\n\n**And the NOSIBLE preview is more revealing than the card suggests.** Their `netloc` values: `zacks.com`, `fool.com`, `benzinga.com`, `investing.com`, `tradingview.com`, `simplywall.st`, `stocktitan.net`, `rttnews.com`, `hl.co.uk`, `menafn.com`, `ogj.com`, `offshore-mag.com`, `worldconstructionnetwork.com`. That's financial news, trade press, stock-analysis sites and press-release wires — **not a random web sample**.\n\nThat reframes your question. NOSIBLE's shards are coherent partly *because their corpus is query-curated news*, not because their clustering is magic. If we cluster raw FineWeb-2 — a broad web sample — our shards will be mushier, and we'd wrongly blame the algorithm. **Corpus composition is a shard-quality lever, not just a scale knob.**\n\nSince both datasets expose the needed columns, there's a move available: extract the `netloc` distribution across all 300k NOSIBLE rows and filter FineWeb-2's `url` to match. That reproduces their corpus *composition* from the only public trace of it. Caveat — those 300k rows were sampled with *finance* queries, so they show the finance slice of their feeds, not the whole index. Their own worked example is gene editing. Domain-matching alone would overfit to finance; it's a seed, not the whole recipe.\n\n## Where quality actually comes from\n\nShard quality decomposes, and different sources fix different parts:\n\n| Dimension | What breaks without it | Best source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Entity index** (stage 5 entity selector, Aho-Corasick tagger) | Entity similarity is a stub | **Wikidata** — CC0, millions of entities, multilingual aliases |\n| **Synonym graph** (stage 7 expansion) | Expansion is guesswork | **Wikipedia redirects** — human-curated aliases, free |\n| **Cluster coherence** | Mushy shards; stages 5–7 look broken | **CC-News** or netloc-matched FineWeb-2 |\n| **Real queries** (stages 1–4, shard `Queries` field) | Every query is synthetic | **ORCAS** — 10M real Bing query→doc pairs |\n| **Company entities** (finance vertical) | No ticker/issuer binding | **GLEIF LEI** + **SEC EDGAR** tickers, both open |\n| **The blog's own example** | Gene-editing query has no documents | **S2ORC / PubMed** |\n| **Event layer / point-in-time** | No temporal network | **GDELT** — free, dated, 15-min updates |\n\nMy ranking by leverage per unit of effort: **Wikidata first** — it converts the entity selector from a stub into a real ranking factor, it's CC0, and it feeds the Aho-Corasick tagger we now know is real in production. **Wikipedia second** — redirects give you a synonym graph for free, articles give clean multilingual clusters, and it's the open stand-in for the Wikipedia/LinkedIn/Market-API Resolver they describe. **ORCAS third**, because it partly dissolves the tension you resolved earlier: real queries mean the generated-eval track carries less weight."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":147365,"output_tokens":4064,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4064,"cache_read_input_tokens":147365,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvkrHtDLmaU1eTSDkzD","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e1a85d2-86d9-4047-9fc3-3b3d8b1beb55","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:00:06.235Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4e1a85d2-86d9-4047-9fc3-3b3d8b1beb55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpvksdVgde6e65uB8fdz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016MqWSKdgRT2d9LV9WKsuzQ","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Which enhancement sources should we adopt? (pick all that apply)","header":"Sources","multiSelect":true,"options":[{"label":"Wikidata (entity backbone)","description":"CC0. Millions of entities with multilingual aliases. Feeds the stage-5 entity sparse selector and the Aho-Corasick per-shard tagger that the research page confirms is in production. Highest leverage per unit of effort."},{"label":"Wikipedia (synonyms + clean clusters)","description":"Redirects are human-curated aliases, giving a real synonym graph for stage 7. Articles give topically coherent multilingual clusters and entity descriptions. Open stand-in for their Resolver Agent's sources."},{"label":"ORCAS real query logs","description":"10M real Bing query-to-document pairs, free for research. Gives genuine queries for stages 1-4 and the per-shard Queries field, reducing how much the generated-eval track has to carry."},{"label":"CC-News / netloc-matched FineWeb-2","description":"Make the corpus news-shaped like NOSIBLE's actual distribution rather than a broad web sample, so cluster coherence reflects their design rather than our input mismatch."}]},{"question":"How should corpus composition be decided?","header":"Composition","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Seed from NOSIBLE netlocs, then broaden (Recommended)","description":"Extract the domain distribution from all 300k NOSIBLE rows as a known-good anchor, then deliberately add topical breadth (science, general news, multilingual) so shards span more than finance. Matches their real composition without overfitting to the finance sample."},{"label":"Pure netloc match","description":"Filter FineWeb-2 strictly to domains seen in the NOSIBLE datasets. Highest fidelity to the one public trace of their corpus, but overfits to finance and would leave the blog's gene-editing example unanswerable."},{"label":"Broad multilingual sample","description":"Take a stratified FineWeb-2 sample across languages and topics with no domain matching. Simplest and most general, but shards will be less coherent than NOSIBLE's and the comparison becomes unfair to our own clustering."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":147365,"output_tokens":4064,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4064,"cache_read_input_tokens":147365,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpvkrHtDLmaU1eTSDkzD","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4fa57a9-307f-4987-aaf1-9446e6a40708","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:00:15.474Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
