{"parentUuid":"909310f2-7bf4-4560-a857-5df9783233bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpwBvoShANkfKUgPUZSx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found the pieces, and they point to amending the spine decision.\n\n**CC-News is the realistic answer.** Available and current:\n\n| Dataset | Coverage | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| `stanford-oval/ccnews` | 2016 → Jun 2024, 100+ languages | Cleaned, deduplicated, language-tagged |\n| `AbedGarra/ccnews2024plus` | Jun 2024 → Jul 2026 | Same pipeline, extends to now |\n| `hotchpotch/multilingual_cc_news` | 100M–1B rows, per-language subsets | Updated Jun 2026 |\n| `brian-learns/cdx-cc-news` | URL index, MIT | **Query which domains exist before downloading** |\n\nThat last one is the unlock for your netloc idea — a CDXj index means we can find NOSIBLE's specific domains inside CC-News without pulling the whole corpus first.\n\nThis is a closer match to NOSIBLE on every axis that matters: news-shaped rather than general web, dated (their point-in-time network), 100+ languages across 150+ countries, and continuously extended the way a crawl is. FineWeb-2 would drop from spine to filler — useful where CC-News is thin in a language, and for non-news reference text.\n\n**The honest cost: licensing gets murkier.** FineWeb-2 is cleanly ODC-By. The CC-News derivatives are mostly `license:unknown` (`Geralt-Targaryen/CC-News` is Apache-2.0 but English-only, 2016–2021). NOSIBLE themselves rely on search-engine fair-use doctrine for their crawl rather than a data licence — which is coherent for them and less so for a repo that publishes artifacts. Your locked decision 3 was emphatic about attribution and licence files, so this genuinely cuts against it.\n\nOne more consequence worth naming: MIRACL is Wikipedia-derived, so its qrels won't judge a news corpus. It stays as a **separately indexed benchmark collection** — which is exactly what your \"clearly separated namespaces\" decision already implies, so nothing breaks, but the real-qrels track will be measuring a different corpus than the one shards are learned over."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7365,"cache_read_input_tokens":156129,"output_tokens":2608,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7365,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2608,"cache_read_input_tokens":156129,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7365},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpwBu7jyGqHmsidsZqbV","attributionMcpServer":"huggingface","attributionMcpTool":"hub_repo_search","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ef073d2-2290-4bf5-ae59-167057f98a91","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:05:34.658Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
