{"parentUuid":"8d1daf0f-fd9d-4897-b87b-4c262d0dc34c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdpzcseyfa9uiAJwfLPNE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":166266,"output_tokens":1809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":166266,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpzcniKbpNR5UUQygMj7","type":"assistant","uuid":"547f9e2b-b3ba-4098-a97a-6ea5898882a2","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:50:03.601Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"547f9e2b-b3ba-4098-a97a-6ea5898882a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdpzcseyfa9uiAJwfLPNE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0127HsNgJthM8ZxZH2B5B7pq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini/.omc/wiki/cybernaut-mini-scope-decisions-2026-07-28.md","old_string":"## Open questions (as of 2026-08-08)","new_string":"8. **Corpus spine — CC-News, not FineWeb-2. Corpus composition is a\n   SHARD-QUALITY lever, not just a scale knob.**\n\n   *The insight:* NOSIBLE's shards are coherent partly because their corpus is\n   query-curated *news*, not a random web sample. Preview of\n   `NOSIBLE/financial-sentiment` `netloc` values — `zacks.com`, `fool.com`,\n   `benzinga.com`, `investing.com`, `tradingview.com`, `simplywall.st`,\n   `stocktitan.net`, `rttnews.com`, `hl.co.uk`, `menafn.com`, `ogj.com`,\n   `offshore-mag.com` — is financial news, trade press, stock-analysis sites and\n   PR wires. Clustering a general web sample would produce mushier shards and we\n   would wrongly blame our clustering algorithm.\n\n   | Role | Dataset | Note |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | Spine | `stanford-oval/ccnews` | 2016–Jun 2024, 100+ langs, cleaned/deduped |\n   | Spine (recency) | `AbedGarra/ccnews2024plus` | Jun 2024→Jul 2026, same pipeline |\n   | Domain targeting | `brian-learns/cdx-cc-news` | MIT URL index — find NOSIBLE's netlocs WITHOUT downloading the whole corpus |\n   | Filler | `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2` | Thin languages, non-news reference text |\n   | Benchmark (separate index) | `miracl/miracl-corpus` + qrels | Wikipedia-derived |\n\n   Matches NOSIBLE on every axis that matters: news-shaped, dated (their\n   point-in-time network), 100+ languages / 150+ countries, continuously\n   extended like a real crawl.\n\n   - **Composition method:** seed domain weighting from the `netloc` distribution\n     across all 300k NOSIBLE rows (the only public trace of their corpus), then\n     broaden deliberately — those rows were sampled with *finance* queries and\n     represent one slice, while the blog's own worked example is gene editing.\n     Seed, not whole recipe.\n   - **ACCEPTED COST — licensing gets murkier.** FineWeb-2 is cleanly ODC-By;\n     CC-News derivatives are mostly `license:unknown`. NOSIBLE relies on\n     search-engine fair-use doctrine for their crawl rather than a data licence.\n     User chose fidelity over provenance clarity with this flagged. Document it;\n     do not publish derived corpus artifacts without revisiting.\n   - **Consequence:** MIRACL qrels judge a Wikipedia corpus, not the news spine,\n     so the real-qrels track measures a *different collection* than the one\n     shards are learned over. Consistent with amendment 7's separate namespaces,\n     but never report the two as one number.\n\n9. **Every source must be config-swappable — no hardcoded corpus.** User: \"and\n   then configs allowing other choices.\" CC-News is the *default*, not a\n   commitment. Follow the pattern already set by the trade shard (`4531e4f`):\n   all I/O owned by the Kedro catalog, sources selected in `parameters.yml`, so\n   swapping CC-News → FineWeb-2 → Wikipedia → a licensed feed touches config\n   only, never pipeline code. Enrichment sources (Wikidata, Wikipedia,\n   ORCAS) are independently toggleable so their contribution to shard quality\n   can be ablated — which is also what makes them *teachable* under the\n   learning mandate.\n\n10. **Enrichment sources adopted — all four.** Each targets a distinct\n    shard-quality dimension:\n    | Dimension | Broken without it | Source |\n    |---|---|---|\n    | Entity index (stage 5 entity selector, Aho-Corasick tagger) | Entity similarity is a stub | **Wikidata** (CC0, multilingual aliases) |\n    | Synonym graph (stage 7 expansion) | Expansion is guesswork | **Wikipedia redirects** (human-curated aliases) |\n    | Cluster coherence | Mushy shards; stages 5–7 look broken | **CC-News / netloc-matched sampling** |\n    | Real queries (stages 1–4, shard `Queries` field) | Every query synthetic | **ORCAS** (10M real Bing query→doc pairs) |\n    ORCAS partly relieves amendment 7's tension: real queries mean the\n    generated-eval track carries less evidential weight.\n\n## Open questions (as of 2026-08-08)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":166266,"output_tokens":1809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":166266,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpzcniKbpNR5UUQygMj7","type":"assistant","uuid":"6b9e1b7c-6018-49b8-b4a9-f63cbe0188c2","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:50:24.333Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
