d (their\n   point-in-time network), 100+ languages / 150+ countries, continuously\n   extended like a real crawl.\n\n   - **Composition method:** seed domain weighting from the `netloc` distribution\n     across all 300k NOSIBLE rows (the only public trace of their corpus), then\n     broaden deliberately — those rows were sampled with *finance* queries and\n     represent one slice, while the blog's own worked example is gene editing.\n     Seed, not whole recipe.\n   - **ACCEPTED COST — licensing gets murkier.** FineWeb-2 is cleanly ODC-By;\n     CC-News derivatives are mostly `license:unknown`. NOSIBLE relies on\n     search-engine fair-use doctrine for their crawl rather than a data licence.\n     User chose fidelity over provenance clarity with this flagged. Document it;\n     do not publish derived corpus artifacts without revisiting.\n   - **Consequence:** MIRACL qrels judge a Wikipedia corpus, not the news spine,\n     so the real-qrels track measures a *different collection* than the one\n     shards are learned over. Consistent with amendment 7's separate namespaces,\n     but never report the two as one number.\n\n9. **Every source must be config-swappable — no hardcoded corpus.** User: \"and\n   then configs allowing other choices.\" CC-News is the *default*, not a\n   commitment. Follow the pattern already set by the trade shard (`4531e4f`):\n   all I/O owned by the Kedro catalog, sources selected in `parameters.yml`, so\n   swapping CC-News → FineWeb-2 → Wikipedia → a licensed feed touches config\n   only, never pipeline code. Enrichment sources (Wikidata, Wikipedia,\n   ORCAS) are independently toggleable so their contribution to shard quality\n   can be ablated — which is also what makes them *teachable* under the\n   learning mandate.\n\n10. **Enrichment sources adopted — all four.** Each targets a distinct\n    shard-quality dimension:\n    | Dimension | Broken without it | Source |\n    |---|---|---|\n    | Entity index (stage 5 entity selector, Aho-Corasick tagger) | Entity similarity is a stub | **Wikidata** (CC0, multilingual aliases) |\n    | Synonym graph (stage 7 expansion) | Expansion is guesswork | **Wikipedia redirects** (human-curated aliases) |\n    | Cluster coherence | Mushy shards; stages 5–7 look broken | **CC-News / netloc-matched sampling** |\n    | Real queries (stages 1–4, shard `Queries` field) | Every query synthetic | **ORCAS** (10M real Bing query→doc pairs) |\n    ORCAS partly relieves amendment 7's tension: real queries mean the\n    generated-eval track carries less evidential weight.\n\n## Open questions (as of 2026-08-08)","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":149,"oldLines":6,"newStart":149,"newLines":66,"lines":["      judgments over fabricated documents, and this is neither.","    - The two must never be averaged, merged, or reported as one figure."," ","+8. **Corpus spine — CC-News, not FineWeb-2. Corpus composition is a","+   SHARD-QUALITY lever, not just a scale knob.**","+","+   *The insight:* NOSIBLE's shards are coherent partly because their corpus is","+   query-curated *news*, not a random web sample. Preview of","+   `NOSIBLE/financial-sentiment` `netloc` values — `zacks.com`, `fool.com`,","+   `benzinga.com`, `investing.com`, `tradingview.com`, `simplywall.st`,","+   `stocktitan.net`, `rttnews.com`, `hl.co.uk`, `menafn.com`, `ogj.com`,","+   `offshore-mag.com` — is financial news, trade press, stock-analysis sites and","+   PR wires. Clustering a general web sample would produce mushier shards and we","+   would wrongly blame our clustering algorithm.","+","+   | Role | Dataset | Note |","+   |---|---|---|","+   | Spine | `stanford-oval/ccnews` | 2016–Jun 2024, 100+ langs, cleaned/deduped |","+   | Spine (recency) | `AbedGarra/ccnews2024plus` | Jun 2024→Jul 2026, same pipeline |","+   | Domain targeting | `brian-learns/cdx-cc-news` | MIT URL index — find NOSIBLE's netlocs WITHOUT downloading the whole corpus |","+   | Filler | `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2` | Thin languages, non-news reference text |","+   | Benchmark (separate index) | `miracl/miracl-corpus` + qrels | Wikipedia-derived |","+","+   Matches NOSIBLE on every axis that matters: news-shaped, dated (their","+   point-in-time network), 100+ languages / 150+ countries, continuously","+   extended like a real crawl.","+","+   - **Composition method:** seed domain weighting from the `netloc` distribution","+     across all 300k NOSIBLE rows (the only public trace of their corpus), then","+     broaden deliberately — those rows were sampled with *finance* queries and","+     represent one slice, while the blog's own worked example is gene editing.","+     Seed, not whole recipe.","+   - **ACCEPTED COST — licensing gets murkier.** FineWeb-2 is cleanly ODC-By;","+     CC-News derivatives are mostly `license:unknown`. NOSIBLE relies on","+     search-engine fair-use doctrine for their crawl rather than a data licence.","+     User chose fidelity over provenance clarity with this flagged. Document it;","+     do not publish derived corpus artifacts without revisiting.","+   - **Consequence:** MIRACL qrels judge a Wikipedia corpus, not the news spine,","+     so the real-qrels track measures a *different collection* than the one","+     shards are learned over. Consistent with amendment 7's separate namespaces,","+     but never report the two as one number.","+","+9. **Every source must be config-swappable — no hardcoded corpus.** User: \"and","+   then configs allowing other choices.\" CC-News is the *default*, not a","+   commitment. Follow the pattern already set by the trade shard (`4531e4f`):","+   all I/O owned by the Kedro catalog, sources selected in `parameters.yml`, so","+   swapping CC-News → FineWeb-2 → Wikipedia → a licensed feed touches config","+   only, never pipeline code. Enrichment sources (Wikidata, Wikipedia,","+   ORCAS) are independently toggleable so their contribution to shard quality","+   can be ablated — which is also what makes them *teachable* under the","+   learning mandate.","+","+10. **Enrichment sources adopted — all four.** Each targets a distinct","+    shard-quality dimension:","+    | Dimension | Broken without it | Source |","+    |---|---|---|","+    | Entity index (stage 5 entity selector, Aho-Corasick tagger) | Entity similarity is a stub | **Wikidata** (CC0, multilingual aliases) |","+    | Synonym graph (stage 7 expansion) | Expansion is guesswork | **Wikipedia redirects** (human-curated aliases) |","+    | Cluster coherence | Mushy shards; stages 5–7 look broken | **CC-News / netloc-matched sampling** |","+    | Real queries (stages 1–4, shard `Queries` field) | Every query synthetic | **ORCAS** (10M real Bing query→doc pairs) |","+    ORCAS partly relieves amendment 7's tension: real queries mean the","+    generated-eval track carries less evidential weight.","+"," ## Open questions (as of 2026-08-08)"," "," - **Shard-size assumption — RESOLVED ENOUGH TO BUILD (web cross-check"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6b9e1b7c-6018-49b8-b4a9-f63cbe0188c2","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspaces/cybernaut_mini","sessionId":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","version":"2.1.223","gitBranch":"main"}
