{"parentUuid":"d35a27b4-c45b-44ba-b638-e18ba505afc1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6e118f93-60b9-44f1-8781-7f5eabf90b16","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bra5fcDfynYJ8ynzxChUEF","type":"tool_result","content":"=== parameters.yml ===\n# Kedro-side defaults. The Typer CLI passes the chosen configs/*.yaml as extra_params,\n# which override these at run time.\n#\n# Paths are NOT parameters any more — they live in conf/base/catalog.yml and are\n# overridden per run via `${runtime_params:...}` (the CLI's --input / --index flags)\n# or per environment via `--env prod`.\n#\n# These defaults deliberately do NOT mirror configs/default.yaml: that file is the\n# quality profile and selects sentence_transformers, which lives behind the optional\n# 'st' extra. A bare `kedro run` must work on the default install, so the baseline\n# here is the offline hash embedder. Opt into real embeddings explicitly with\n# `--config configs/default.yaml` (CLI) or `--env prod` (Kedro).\nseed: 42\nembedding:\n  # Deterministic feature hashing — no download, no extra, works offline. A\n  # first-class provider, not a stub.\n  provider: hash\n  # Used only when provider is 'sentence_transformers'.\n  model: intfloat/multilingual-e5-small\n  # Commit SHA of the model weights. null resolves to the repo's default branch,\n  # which is fine locally but not reproducible: two builds months apart can embed\n  # with different tensors and silently yield a different index from one corpus.\n  # Production builds must pin it — see conf/prod/parameters.yml.\n  revision: null\n  dim: 256\nindex:\n  n_shards: 12\n  max_keywords: 30\n  max_entities: 30\n  cooccurrence_window: 5\n  min_edge_count: 2\nrrf:\n  k: 60\n  dense_weight: 1.0\n  lexical_weight: 1.0\n  entity_weight: 0.5\nagent:\n  exploration_constant: 1.2\n  max_expansions: 5\n  max_retrieval_calls: 18\n  judge: heuristic\n  query_generator: heuristic\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n# corpus_ingest                                                       #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n\n# How raw source rows map onto the Document schema. Retarget a different source by\n# changing this mapping, not the normaliser.\ncorpus:\n  field_map:\n    text: text\n    url: url\n  metadata_fields: []\n  default_language: en\n  id_prefix: doc\n  min_text_chars: 32\n\n# Narrowing applied between the intermediate and primary layers.\ncorpus_selection:\n  languages: null\n  metadata_equals: null\n  max_documents: null\n\n# Set by the CLI (or `kedro run --params offline=true`) per invocation.\noffline: false\n\n=== catalog.yml (first 60) ===\n# Data catalog — the single place that knows where data lives.\n#\n# Every corpus and index path in the project is declared here rather than opened\n# inside a node, so `kedro viz` renders true lineage and swapping a local corpus\n# for a Hugging Face one is a config change (`--env prod`), not a code change.\n#\n# Layers follow the Kedro convention:\n#   01_raw          verbatim source rows, exactly as fetched\n#   02_intermediate mapped onto the Document schema\n#   03_primary      filtered and capped: the corpus a build actually consumes\n#   08_reporting    evaluation output\n#\n# `${runtime_params:name,default}` lets the Typer CLI keep its --input / --index\n# flags: those flags are forwarded as Kedro runtime params and resolve here.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n# 01_raw — acquisition                                                #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n\n# Default source is a local file so `kedro run --pipeline corpus_ingest` never\n# touches the network unless the prod environment overrides it.\nraw_corpus_source:\n  type: cybernaut_mini.datasets.JsonlDataset\n  filepath: ${runtime_params:raw_source_path,data/01_raw/corpus_source.jsonl}\n\nraw_corpus:\n  type: cybernaut_mini.datasets.JsonlDataset\n  filepath: data/01_raw/corpus_snapshot.jsonl\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n# 02_intermediate — normalised to the Document schema                 #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n\nnormalized_documents:\n  type: cybernaut_mini.datasets.JsonlDataset\n  filepath: data/02_intermediate/documents.jsonl\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n# 03_primary — the build-ready corpus                                 #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n\n# corpus_ingest WRITES this and index_build reads it, so its default must be a\n# generated path. It must never default into data/sample/: that directory holds a\n# committed fixture, and an acquisition run would overwrite it.\n# Sample builds reach the fixture by passing it explicitly —\n# `cybernaut-mini build --input data/sample/documents.jsonl` — which arrives here\n# as the input_path runtime param.\ndocuments:\n  type: cybernaut_mini.datasets.JsonlDataset\n  filepath: ${runtime_params:input_path,data/03_primary/corpus.jsonl}\n\njudgments:\n  type: cybernaut_mini.datasets.JsonlDataset\n  filepath: ${runtime_params:judgments_path,data/sample/judgments.jsonl}\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n# The index                                                           #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n\n# One catalog entry for the whole index directory. `save` performs the canonical","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3a0872ae-5b2c-45e0-bd86-382177f2f898","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:50:29.469Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== parameters.yml ===\n# Kedro-side defaults. The Typer CLI passes the chosen configs/*.yaml as extra_params,\n# which override these at run time.\n#\n# Paths are NOT parameters any more — they live in conf/base/catalog.yml and are\n# overridden per run