{"parentUuid":"43ac578b-ba1c-48bf-a417-8795596615c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdpzg8H8sByeXXwwodMyy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two findings in the existing config change the picture — one is more important than any data source.\n\n## The biggest shard-quality lever is already in the repo, and it's broken\n\n`conf/base/parameters.yml` defaults to `embedding.provider: hash`, described in-comment as *\"A first-class provider, not a stub.\"* `HashEmbedder` is still live in `src/cybernaut_mini/providers/embeddings.py` and `config.py:31` types the provider as `Literal[\"hash\", \"sentence_transformers\"]` with `hash` as default.\n\n**That directly contradicts locked decision 5** (\"hash embedder REMOVED. Real embeddings only\"). It was only half-applied — `conf/prod/parameters.yml` does use `multilingual-e5-small`, but base does not.\n\nThis matters more than any corpus choice: **shards are learned by clustering embeddings.** Cluster feature-hashed vectors and you get incoherent shards no matter how good the corpus is, because a hash embedder has no semantic structure to cluster on. Stages 5–7 would look broken and we'd blame the algorithm — the same failure mode as the corpus-composition issue, one layer down. Adding Wikidata and CC-News on top of a hash embedder would be wasted effort.\n\nEncouraging convergence though: `conf/prod/parameters.yml` sets `n_shards: 64` with the comment *\"~2k documents per shard at this scale\"* — which lands inside the 1,000–4,000 docs/shard range the research page implies. Whoever wrote that reasoned to the same place independently.\n\nAlso worth noting: `src/cybernaut_mini/edgar/` already exists, so one of the enrichment sources is partly built, and `sharding.py` is already a module.\n\n## The config shape\n\nThe repo's convention is established and fits your ask exactly — `catalog.yml` says *\"swapping a local corpus for a Hugging Face one is a config change, not a code change\"* and `corpus.field_map` says *\"Retarget a different source by changing this mapping, not the normaliser.\"* So:\n\n```yaml\ncorpus:\n  source: ccnews                 # <- the only line you change to swap spine\n  sources:\n    ccnews:\n      repo: stanford-oval/ccnews\n      recency_repo: AbedGarra/ccnews2024plus\n      field_map: {text: text, url: url, date: date}\n      netloc_seed: data/01_raw/nosible_netlocs.txt   # from the 300k rows\n    fineweb2:\n      repo: HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2\n      field_map: {text: text, url: url, date: date, language: language}\n    miracl:\n      repo: miracl/miracl-corpus     # benchmark namespace, indexed separately\n\nenrichment:                      # independently toggleable for ablation\n  wikidata:  {enabled: true,  aliases: multilingual}\n  wikipedia: {enabled: true,  use_redirects: true}\n  orcas:     {enabled: true}\n```\n\nEach enrichment toggling independently is what lets you *measure* its contribution to shard coherence — which is also what makes it teachable under the learning mandate, rather than a pile of sources asserted to help."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1891,"cache_read_input_tokens":171947,"output_tokens":2591,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1891,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2591,"cache_read_input_tokens":171947,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1891},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdpzg6NHyf8QRcCDqTdQK","type":"assistant","uuid":"bdbded5a-9173-4761-a3f2-7eaf84a2fce2","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:51:10.846Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1739850f-85bf-4d10-b02b-a0b2492e7df8","u